.vercel

# Next 16 writes these into the app directory on every `next dev` and
# `next build` (see node_modules/next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js),
# so they are generated output rather than source. Keeping them untracked and
# ignored is what stops them dirtying the tree. next-env.d.ts, written by the
# same code path, is covered by the root .gitignore.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Playwright output from `npm run test:e2e`.
playwright-report/
test-results/
